      "description": "Pictures of a changed figure, diagram or table, before and after, and how much of it changed. Says when to use it, what the percentage means and must NOT be read as, what a missing picture means, and how the staging job and the review process call it. Use when a reviewer asks \"what does this figure look like now\", when a table's markup diff is unreadable, or when a staging preview's pictures are missing.",
